A no-config Anthropic run now uses claude-opus-5-5 instead of the older claude-opus-4-6, and --help builds its default from the code instead of a hard-coded string. Build, tests, clippy, fmt and tests/harness_logic.sh (212 passed) are all green. It's committed as e7a33c5b.

Why `claude-opus-5-5`: I checked three things before changing it (step 1 of the plan):
• Preset: it has its own entry in anthropic_preset, with a 1M window and a 64K default for max_tokens.
• Price: yoagent's price table has it at $4/$20, which is cheaper than the $5/$25 Opus 4.6 it replaces. The plan expected "the same price tier"; it's actually below it, and the comment above the default says so.
• Output limit: with no config, no max_tokens is set, so the run sends the preset's 64K. That's under the model's 128,000 maximum.

What changed:
• `src/providers.rs`: the fallback default is now claude-opus-5-5, with a comment saying it's a decision and listing the three checks. A new test runs those same checks against whatever the default is, and also checks it doesn't set off the unknown-model warning.
• `src/help.rs`: the --model line now shows default_model_for_provider("anthropic"), and a test checks the exact line.
• `src/setup.rs`: the setup-wizard test compares against that function instead of a fixed string.
• Docs: I updated the lines that state the default in models.md (intro, the anthropic row, and the custom row, which uses the same fallback), installation.md, the quick-start.md banner, and fork.md. I left the example config at models.md:83 and the dated measurements alone.

Checked in an empty temp dir with no config:
```
yoyo (prompt mode) — model: claude-opus-5-5
PONG
  --model <name>    Model to use (default: claude-opus-5-5)
```

Still open on #1037: openai (gpt-5), openrouter and bedrock (claude-sonnet-4-6) and 7 unchecked providers still default without a stated decision. That sentence is in the commit body and in a comment on #1037. While editing I also saw that installation.md and fork.md list gpt-4o as the OpenAI default, but the code says gpt-5. That's part of the openai work, so I didn't touch it.
